{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794865352247,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"id":"prt_1e64fce37001RlmBFBdqk8N7En","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e64fc2e8001QxSZatk1Gh9pN4","type":"step-start","snapshot":"b1b966923c6d4213f5e02c3f91a98a53a2a66f86"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865352843,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e64fcefb002Op9Aqz4ToNLzmk","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e64fc2e8001QxSZatk1Gh9pN4","type":"tool","id":"call_12950da33681407cb34c8a94","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":500,"offset":1783,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1783-2282\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1861:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1862:         applies_to: confirm\n1863:         type: approval_gate\n1864:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1865:         present: |\n1866:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1867: \n1868:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1869:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1870:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1871:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1872:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1873: \n1874:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1875: \n1876:           Options:\n1877:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1878:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1879:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1880:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1881:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1882:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1883:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1884:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1885: \n1886:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1887:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1888:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1889:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1890: \n1891:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1892:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1893:         algorithm: |\n1894:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1895:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1896:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1897:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1898:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1899:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1900:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1901:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1902:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1903:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1904:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1905:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1906:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1907:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1908:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1909:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1910:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1911:              - Determine final severity and status\n1912:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only: step_derive_verdict reads the registry file after the self-check refreshes it, and the report and the closeout state its counts as the counts the verdict used.\n1913:         outputs:\n1914:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1915: \n1916:       # Adjudication persistence: the Referee's call becomes a claim_adjudication row per\n1917:       # finding, so the registry the verdict reads carries the final severity. A false\n1918:       # positive is recorded as `none`, the scale value for a claim that is not a finding.\n1919:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1920:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1921:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1922:         algorithm: |\n1923:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1924:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1925:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1926:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1927:           Record one `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair for every call the Referee made\n1928:           here: the severity it settled on, or `none` when it called the finding a false\n1929:           positive. An empty list means the Referee changed nothing.\n1930:           On a single-executor run, append one deep_review.claim_adjudication row per pair\n1931:           through the gateway, then refresh the registry once. The verdict step that\n1932:           follows reads the refreshed registry, so a downgrade or a false positive changes\n1933:           the counts the verdict, the report and the closeout all use.\n1934:           On a fan-out root, record the pairs for the report only: the root has no state\n1935:           log before closeout, and the merged lineage counts are what that verdict reads.\n1936:         extract:\n1937:           - selfcheck_adjudications: \"One `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair per line, using the findingId exactly as it appears in openFindings of {state_paths.findings_registry}, empty when the Referee changed nothing\"\n1938:           - adjudication_mode: \"`mode` of the latest claim_adjudication gate row (the newest one without a findingId), else \\\"review\\\"\"\n1939:           - adjudication_run: \"`run` of that gate row, else {highest_run}\"\n1940:           - adjudication_passed: \"`passed` of that gate row, else true\"\n1941:           - adjudication_active_p0_p1: \"`activeP0P1` of that gate row, else {p0_count} plus {p1_count}\"\n1942:           - adjudication_missing_packets: \"`missingPackets` of that gate row as a JSON array, else []\"\n1943:           - adjudication_reason: \"`reason` of that gate row as a JSON value, else \\\"adversarial self-check\\\"\"\n1944:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1945:         if_present:\n1946:           action: \"Record the pairs in the Executive Summary for reference. Do not append: a fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, and each lineage already adjudicated its own findings, so the merged counts are the authority here.\"\n1947:         if_absent:\n1948:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1949:           # ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh.\n1950:           command: |\n1951:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1952:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1953:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n1954:             while read -r FINDING_ID FINAL_SEVERITY; do\n1955:             [ -n \"$FINDING_ID\" ] || continue\n1956:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1957:             cat <<DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1958:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"{adjudication_mode}\",\"run\":{adjudication_run},\"passed\":{adjudication_passed},\"activeP0P1\":{adjudication_active_p0_p1},\"missingPackets\":{adjudication_missing_packets},\"reason\":{adjudication_reason},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"findingId\":\"$FINDING_ID\",\"finalSeverity\":\"$FINAL_SEVERITY\"}}\n1959:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1960:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$RUN_DIR\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1961:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1962:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1963:             [ \"$RECORD_STATUS\" -eq 0 ] || exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1964:             done <<'DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS'\n1965:             {selfcheck_adjudications}\n1966:             DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS\n1967:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1968:           on_fail:\n1969:             action: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. An append the gateway rejected leaves the ledger and the registry disagreeing, so the verdict that follows would read a stale count.\"\n1970:             halt: true\n1971:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1972:           log: \"Adversarial self-check adjudicated {selfcheck_adjudications}; the verdict reads the refreshed registry.\"\n1973: \n1974:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1975:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1976:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1977:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1978:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1979:       step_derive_verdict:\n1980:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1981:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1982:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1983:         if_present:\n1984:           command: |\n1985:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1986:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1987:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1988:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1989:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1990:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1991:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1992:           wait_for_completion: true\n1993:           bind_from_output:\n1994:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1995:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2176:       gate_post_synthesis:\n2177:         applies_to: confirm\n2178:         type: approval_gate\n2179:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2180:         present: |\n2181:           ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2182: \n2183:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2184:           **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2185:           **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2186:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2187: \n2188:           Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2189: \n2190:           Options:\n2191:           A) Approve and save to memory\n2192:           B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2193:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2194:           D) Skip memory save\n2195:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n2196:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2197:         on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2198:         on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2199:         on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2200:         on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2201: \n2202:   # ════════\n2203:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2204:   # ════════\n2205:   phase_save:\n2206:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2207:     steps:\n2208: \n2209:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2210:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2211:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2212:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2213:         requirements:\n2214:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2215:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans, and a full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four.\"\n2216:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2217:         example_payload: |\n2218:           {\n2219:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2220:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2221:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2222:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2223:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2224:             \"toolCalls\": [],\n2225:             \"recent_action\": \"Deep review finished with verdict {verdict} after {iteration_count} iterations\",\n2226:             \"next_safe_action\": \"Act on the verdict in review/review-report.md\",\n2227:             \"blockers\": [],\n2228:             \"key_files\": [\"review/review-report.md\"]\n2229:           }\n2230: \n2231:       step_generate_context:\n2232:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2233:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2234:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\"\n2235:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2236: \n2237:       step_verify_save:\n2238:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2239:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2240:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2241: \n2242:       step_release_lock:\n2243:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2244:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2245:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2246:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2247: \n2248:   # ════════\n2249:   # COMPLETION\n2250:   # ════════\n2251:   completion:\n2252:     message: |\n2253:       Deep review complete.\n2254:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2255:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2256:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2257: \n2258:       Artifacts:\n2259:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2260:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2261:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2262:         - Memory context saved\n2263: \n2264:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2265:     next_steps:\n2266:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2267:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2268:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2269:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2270: \n2271: # ────────\n2272: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2273: # ────────\n2274: error_recovery:\n2275:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2276:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2277:   consecutive_failures: \"See step_check_convergence rule 1a. The script counts trailing failed iterations from the state log and returns stop reason error.\"\n2278:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2279: \n2280: # ────────\n2281: # RULES\n2282: # ────────\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2283]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1783-2282\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1861:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1862:         applies_to: confirm\n1863:         type: approval_gate\n1864:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1865:         present: |\n1866:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1867: \n1868:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1869:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1870:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1871:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1872:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1873: \n1874:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1875: \n1876:           Options:\n1877:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1878:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1879:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1880:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1881:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1882:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1883:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1884:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1885: \n1886:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1887:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1888:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1889:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1890: \n1891:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1892:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1893:         algorithm: |\n1894:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1895:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1896:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1897:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1898:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1899:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1900:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1901:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1902:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1903:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1904:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1905:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1906:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1907:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1908:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1909:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1910:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1911:              - Determine final severity and status\n1912:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only: step_derive_verdict reads the registry file after the self-check refreshes it, and the report and the closeout state its counts as the counts the verdict used.\n1913:         outputs:\n1914:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1915: \n1916:       # Adjudication persistence: the Referee's call becomes a claim_adjudication row per\n1917:       # finding, so the registry the verdict reads carries the final severity. A false\n1918:       # positive is recorded as `none`, the scale value for a claim that is not a finding.\n1919:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1920:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1921:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1922:         algorithm: |\n1923:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1924:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1925:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1926:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1927:           Record one `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair for every call the Referee made\n1928:           here: the severity it settled on, or `none` when it called the finding a false\n1929:           positive. An empty list means the Referee changed nothing.\n1930:           On a single-executor run, append one deep_review.claim_adjudication row per pair\n1931:           through the gateway, then refresh the registry once. The verdict step that\n1932:           follows reads the refreshed registry, so a downgrade or a false positive changes\n1933:           the counts the verdict, the report and the closeout all use.\n1934:           On a fan-out root, record the pairs for the report only: the root has no state\n1935:           log before closeout, and the merged lineage counts are what that verdict reads.\n1936:         extract:\n1937:           - selfcheck_adjudications: \"One `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair per line, using the findingId exactly as it appears in openFindings of {state_paths.findings_registry}, empty when the Referee changed nothing\"\n1938:           - adjudication_mode: \"`mode` of the latest claim_adjudication gate row (the newest one without a findingId), else \\\"review\\\"\"\n1939:           - adjudication_run: \"`run` of that gate row, else {highest_run}\"\n1940:           - adjudication_passed: \"`passed` of that gate row, else true\"\n1941:           - adjudication_active_p0_p1: \"`activeP0P1` of that gate row, else {p0_count} plus {p1_count}\"\n1942:           - adjudication_missing_packets: \"`missingPackets` of that gate row as a JSON array, else []\"\n1943:           - adjudication_reason: \"`reason` of that gate row as a JSON value, else \\\"adversarial self-check\\\"\"\n1944:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1945:         if_present:\n1946:           action: \"Record the pairs in the Executive Summary for reference. Do not append: a fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, and each lineage already adjudicated its own findings, so the merged counts are the authority here.\"\n1947:         if_absent:\n1948:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1949:           # ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh.\n1950:           command: |\n1951:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1952:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1953:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n1954:             while read -r FINDING_ID FINAL_SEVERITY; do\n1955:             [ -n \"$FINDING_ID\" ] || continue\n1956:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1957:             cat <<DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1958:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"{adjudication_mode}\",\"run\":{adjudication_run},\"passed\":{adjudication_passed},\"activeP0P1\":{adjudication_active_p0_p1},\"missingPackets\":{adjudication_missing_packets},\"reason\":{adjudication_reason},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"findingId\":\"$FINDING_ID\",\"finalSeverity\":\"$FINAL_SEVERITY\"}}\n1959:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1960:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$RUN_DIR\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1961:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1962:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1963:             [ \"$RECORD_STATUS\" -eq 0 ] || exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1964:             done <<'DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS'\n1965:             {selfcheck_adjudications}\n1966:             DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS\n1967:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1968:           on_fail:\n1969:             action: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. An append the gateway rejected leaves the ledger and the registry disagreeing, so the verdict that follows would read a stale count.\"\n1970:             halt: true\n1971:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1972:           log: \"Adversarial self-check adjudicated {selfcheck_adjudications}; the verdict reads the refreshed registry.\"\n1973: \n1974:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1975:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1976:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1977:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1978:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1979:       step_derive_verdict:\n1980:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1981:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1982:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1983:         if_present:\n1984:           command: |\n1985:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1986:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1987:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1988:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1989:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1990:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1991:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1992:           wait_for_completion: true\n1993:           bind_from_output:\n1994:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1995:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2176:       gate_post_synthesis:\n2177:         applies_to: confirm\n2178:         type: approval_gate\n2179:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2180:         present: |\n2181:           ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2182: \n2183:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2184:           **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2185:           **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2186:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2187: \n2188:           Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2189: \n2190:           Options:\n2191:           A) Approve and save to memory\n2192:           B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2193:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2194:           D) Skip memory save\n2195:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n2196:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2197:         on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2198:         on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2199:         on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2200:         on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2201: \n2202:   # ════════\n2203:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2204:   # ════════\n2205:   phase_save:\n2206:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2207:     steps:\n2208: \n2209:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2210:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2211:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2212:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2213:         requirements:\n2214:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2215:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans, and a full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four.\"\n2216:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2217:         example_payload: |\n2218:           {\n2219:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2220:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2221:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2222:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2223:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2224:             \"toolCalls\": [],\n2225:             \"recent_action\": \"Deep review finished with verdict {verdict} after {iteration_count} iterations\",\n2226:             \"next_safe_action\": \"Act on the verdict in review/review-report.md\",\n2227:             \"blockers\": [],\n2228:             \"key_files\": [\"review/review-report.md\"]\n2229:           }\n2230: \n2231:       step_generate_context:\n2232:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2233:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2234:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\"\n2235:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2236: \n2237:       step_verify_save:\n2238:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2239:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2240:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2241: \n2242:       step_release_lock:\n2243:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2244:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2245:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2246:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2247: \n2248:   # ════════\n2249:   # COMPLETION\n2250:   # ════════\n2251:   completion:\n2252:     message: |\n2253:       Deep review complete.\n2254:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2255:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2256:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2257: \n2258:       Artifacts:\n2259:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2260:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2261:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2262:         - Memory context saved\n2263: \n2264:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2265:     next_steps:\n2266:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2267:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2268:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2269:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2270: \n2271: # ────────\n2272: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2273: # ────────\n2274: error_recovery:\n2275:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2276:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2277:   consecutive_failures: \"See step_check_convergence rule 1a. The script counts trailing failed iterations from the state log and returns stop reason error.\"\n2278:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2279: \n2280: # ────────\n2281: # RULES\n2282: # ────────\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2283]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":500,\"offset\":1783,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794865352443,"end":1794865352843}}}}
