{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865601231,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6539477001RiTjs3tbTsZkbJ","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e6537e8f001p0vZsnoFy6IF2k","type":"tool","id":"call_d09df5d4096946bda838a6a3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg --no-config -n 'commandOnlyMentioned|mention|refus|document' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/command-offer-fit-gates.md | head -40"},"output":"3:description: \"Manual validation that advisor_recommend withholds a hub's slash command when the prompt refuses it, asks about it, rules out a change or asks for a small correction, and still names a command row's own command with its policy.\"\n12:Prompt: Manual validation that advisor_recommend withholds a hub's slash command when the prompt refuses it, asks about it, rules out a change or asks for a small correction, and still names a command row's own command with its policy.\n18:A hub route names the command that acts on the mode it picked. That offer is only right when the reader asked for the workflow. A prompt that names the command to refuse it, asks a question about it, rules out a change or asks for a correction inside one existing document is not asking for the workflow, so the offer is withheld.\n22:1. A command the prompt refuses or asks about is a naming, not a request.\n24:3. A correction inside one document is not a request for a creation workflow.\n32:- Objective: Confirm the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates withhold a hub command while a plain request still carries `/create:readme` with `start`, and read a command row's own policy.\n36:- Expected signals: no command on the refusal, the question, the no-edit request and the typo fix, `/create:readme` with `start` on the plain request, and `/doctor:git setup` with `run` on the git prompt's command row.\n51:2. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"do not run /create:readme, just tell me what it covers\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-012-refusal.json`\n63:| NC-012 | Command the prompt does not ask for is not offered | Confirm the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates withhold a hub command while a plain request still carries its command | `Run advisor_recommend on six prompts and check which recommendations carry a command and its policy word.` | Commands 1 to 8 above | No command on the refusal, the question, the no-edit request and the typo fix. `/create:readme` with `start` on the plain request. `/doctor:git setup` with `run` on the git command row. A single route to `sk-create-readme` on the five readme prompts | The six JSON files plus the terminal transcript | PASS if all six results match. FAIL otherwise | See Failure Triage |\n68:- `nc-012-refusal.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc` with a single route to `sk-create-readme`. It has no `command` key, because `do not run` is a decline lead before the command.\n72:- `nc-012-typo.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc` with a single route to `sk-create-readme`. It has no `command` key, because `typo` and `line 12` mark a correction inside one document rather than a request for a new one.\n106:- **Fail**: a refusal, a question, a no-edit request or a typo fix carries a command, the plain request carries no command or a different policy, or the git command row carries a different command or policy.\n110:1. A refusal or question still carries a command: compare the prompt with `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` and `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, then run `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\n122:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | `commandOnlyMentioned`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING`, plus the mode table that maps `sk-create-readme` to `/create:readme` |\n123:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Regression tests for the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Manual validation that advisor_recommend withholds a hub's slash command when the prompt refuses it, asks about it, rules out a change or asks for a small correction, and still names a command row's own command with its policy.\"\n12:Prompt: Manual validation that advisor_recommend withholds a hub's slash command when the prompt refuses it, asks about it, rules out a change or asks for a small correction, and still names a command row's own command with its policy.\n18:A hub route names the command that acts on the mode it picked. That offer is only right when the reader asked for the workflow. A prompt that names the command to refuse it, asks a question about it, rules out a change or asks for a correction inside one existing document is not asking for the workflow, so the offer is withheld.\n22:1. A command the prompt refuses or asks about is a naming, not a request.\n24:3. A correction inside one document is not a request for a creation workflow.\n32:- Objective: Confirm the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates withhold a hub command while a plain request still carries `/create:readme` with `start`, and read a command row's own policy.\n36:- Expected signals: no command on the refusal, the question, the no-edit request and the typo fix, `/create:readme` with `start` on the plain request, and `/doctor:git setup` with `run` on the git prompt's command row.\n51:2. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"do not run /create:readme, just tell me what it covers\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-012-refusal.json`\n63:| NC-012 | Command the prompt does not ask for is not offered | Confirm the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates withhold a hub command while a plain request still carries its command | `Run advisor_recommend on six prompts and check which recommendations carry a command and its policy word.` | Commands 1 to 8 above | No command on the refusal, the question, the no-edit request and the typo fix. `/create:readme` with `start` on the plain request. `/doctor:git setup` with `run` on the git command row. A single route to `sk-create-readme` on the five readme prompts | The six JSON files plus the terminal transcript | PASS if all six results match. FAIL otherwise | See Failure Triage |\n68:- `nc-012-refusal.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc` with a single route to `sk-create-readme`. It has no `command` key, because `do not run` is a decline lead before the command.\n72:- `nc-012-typo.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc` with a single route to `sk-create-readme`. It has no `command` key, because `typo` and `line 12` mark a correction inside one document rather than a request for a new one.\n106:- **Fail**: a refusal, a question, a no-edit request or a typo fix carries a command, the plain request carries no command or a different policy, or the git command row carries a different command or policy.\n110:1. A refusal or question still carries a command: compare the prompt with `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` and `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, then run `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\n122:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | `commandOnlyMentioned`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING`, plus the mode table that maps `sk-create-readme` to `/create:readme` |\n123:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Regression tests for the refusal, question, no-edit and small-edit gates |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg --no-config -n 'commandOnlyMentioned|mention|refus|document' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/command-offer-fit-gates.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794865599607,"end":1794865601231}}}}
