{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865612745,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e653c5ba001sXoEF0mj53saqX","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e653a95f001YZigqX13VVdcu1","type":"tool","id":"call_7cb83366cf87473fb0eafa61","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md","offset":40,"limit":80},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md, lines 40-119\n40: This is **Phase 40** of the command surfacing build. The full alignment run `20261116T195539Z` on `b8ebee37d75` reported 0 P0, 7 P1 and 24 P2, and review pass twelve kept one P1 as a known limit under a capped close. The operator then chose, through the ask tool on 2026-11-16, the full loop: fix every P1, the mention check ones included, and rerun review and alignment.\n41: \n42: **Scope Boundary**: `commandOnlyMentioned` and `typedCommandIn` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and their guards test, one manual testing playbook scenario, and the advisor's `intent_signals`. No scorer weight, threshold, corpus row, baseline or ledger change.\n43: \n44: **Dependencies**:\n45: - The alignment run's `findings.json` and review pass twelve's `review/review-report.md`\n46: \n47: **Deliverables**:\n48: - The fixes, a failing-first case for each, the gate evidence, review pass thirteen and a fresh alignment run\n49: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: <!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n54: ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n55: \n56: ### Problem Statement\n57: A reader who refuses or questions a command still gets it offered in four shapes: a refusal after the name (\"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"), the command named as a document (\"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"), a wrapper the fold keeps such as `[/create:readme]`, and a doc path such as `/create:readme.md` beside a led refusal. One playbook scenario pins a prompt that no longer tops `/doctor:update`. Four advisor tasks, a stale skill graph rebuild, the Vibe prompt hook setup and the behaviour arena, rank another skill or none first.\n58: \n59: ### Purpose\n60: A refused or questioned command is never offered in those shapes, a request still is, the playbook passes as written, and the four advisor tasks rank the advisor first without moving the floors.\n61: <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n62: \n63: <!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n64: ### Measured Behavior\n65: ```text\n66: $ node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend ... \"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"\n67: {\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}\n68: $ ... \"run /doctor:git setup but do not actually run it\"\n69: {\"skillId\":\"command-doctor-git-setup\",\"command\":\"/doctor:git setup\",\"policy\":\"run\"}\n70: $ ... \"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"\n71: {\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}\n72: commandOnlyMentioned(\"do not run [/create:readme], just explain\", \"/create:readme\") = false (plain form true)\n73: run-probes: P05 top command-doctor-helper, P07 top sk-prompt, P08 top sk-doc, P09 top none (want system-skill-advisor)\n74: Claude hook on \"update skilled to the latest version\": ambiguous sk-git vs sk-doc, no /doctor:update\n75: ```\n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n81: ## 3. SCOPE\n82: \n83: ### In Scope\n84: - Read a refusal of the command after its name (\"do not run it\", \"don't actually run it\")\n85: - Read a command named as a document, file, page or source as a mention\n86: - Drop square brackets, `~~`, `<code>` tags, guillemets and primes in the fold, and widen the typed reader's start boundary to match\n87: - Skip a doc-path occurrence such as `/create:readme.md` in the occurrence scan\n88: - Change the playbook prompt to one that tops `/doctor:update`\n89: - Add advisor `intent_signals` for the four probe tasks\n90: - Run review pass thirteen and a full alignment run\n91: \n92: ### Out of Scope\n93: - Underscore emphasis, because a command name may hold an underscore\n94: - Any scorer weight, threshold, corpus row or baseline change\n95: - Reading holdout prompt text (D6)\n96: \n97: ### Files to Change\n98: \n99: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n100: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n101: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The mention fold, the tail refusal, the document noun, the path skip and the typed start boundary |\n102: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Failing-first cases and the wider wrapper matrix |\n103: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md` | Modify | The third prompt |\n104: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` | Modify | Intent signals for the four probe tasks |\n105: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modify | Recompiled graph |\n106: | `../goal.md` | Modify | Rows through the goal log command only |\n107: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n112: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n113: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n114: \n115: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n116: \n117: | ID | Requirement |\n118: |----|-------------|\n119: | REQ-001 | A refusal after the name, a command named as a document, a wrapper in the wider set and a doc path beside a led refusal each read as a mention, and every request fixture still reads as a request |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md, lines 40-119\n40: This is **Phase 40** of the command surfacing build. The full alignment run `20261116T195539Z` on `b8ebee37d75` reported 0 P0, 7 P1 and 24 P2, and review pass twelve kept one P1 as a known limit under a capped close. The operator then chose, through the ask tool on 2026-11-16, the full loop: fix every P1, the mention check ones included, and rerun review and alignment.\n41: \n42: **Scope Boundary**: `commandOnlyMentioned` and `typedCommandIn` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and their guards test, one manual testing playbook scenario, and the advisor's `intent_signals`. No scorer weight, threshold, corpus row, baseline or ledger change.\n43: \n44: **Dependencies**:\n45: - The alignment run's `findings.json` and review pass twelve's `review/review-report.md`\n46: \n47: **Deliverables**:\n48: - The fixes, a failing-first case for each, the gate evidence, review pass thirteen and a fresh alignment run\n49: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: <!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n54: ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n55: \n56: ### Problem Statement\n57: A reader who refuses or questions a command still gets it offered in four shapes: a refusal after the name (\"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"), the command named as a document (\"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"), a wrapper the fold keeps such as `[/create:readme]`, and a doc path such as `/create:readme.md` beside a led refusal. One playbook scenario pins a prompt that no longer tops `/doctor:update`. Four advisor tasks, a stale skill graph rebuild, the Vibe prompt hook setup and the behaviour arena, rank another skill or none first.\n58: \n59: ### Purpose\n60: A refused or questioned command is never offered in those shapes, a request still is, the playbook passes as written, and the four advisor tasks rank the advisor first without moving the floors.\n61: <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n62: \n63: <!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n64: ### Measured Behavior\n65: ```text\n66: $ node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend ... \"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"\n67: {\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}\n68: $ ... \"run /doctor:git setup but do not actually run it\"\n69: {\"skillId\":\"command-doctor-git-setup\",\"command\":\"/doctor:git setup\",\"policy\":\"run\"}\n70: $ ... \"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"\n71: {\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}\n72: commandOnlyMentioned(\"do not run [/create:readme], just explain\", \"/create:readme\") = false (plain form true)\n73: run-probes: P05 top command-doctor-helper, P07 top sk-prompt, P08 top sk-doc, P09 top none (want system-skill-advisor)\n74: Claude hook on \"update skilled to the latest version\": ambiguous sk-git vs sk-doc, no /doctor:update\n75: ```\n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n81: ## 3. SCOPE\n82: \n83: ### In Scope\n84: - Read a refusal of the command after its name (\"do not run it\", \"don't actually run it\")\n85: - Read a command named as a document, file, page or source as a mention\n86: - Drop square brackets, `~~`, `<code>` tags, guillemets and primes in the fold, and widen the typed reader's start boundary to match\n87: - Skip a doc-path occurrence such as `/create:readme.md` in the occurrence scan\n88: - Change the playbook prompt to one that tops `/doctor:update`\n89: - Add advisor `intent_signals` for the four probe tasks\n90: - Run review pass thirteen and a full alignment run\n91: \n92: ### Out of Scope\n93: - Underscore emphasis, because a command name may hold an underscore\n94: - Any scorer weight, threshold, corpus row or baseline change\n95: - Reading holdout prompt text (D6)\n96: \n97: ### Files to Change\n98: \n99: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n100: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n101: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The mention fold, the tail refusal, the document noun, the path skip and the typed start boundary |\n102: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Failing-first cases and the wider wrapper matrix |\n103: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md` | Modify | The third prompt |\n104: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` | Modify | Intent signals for the four probe tasks |\n105: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modify | Recompiled graph |\n106: | `../goal.md` | Modify | Rows through the goal log command only |\n107: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n112: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n113: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n114: \n115: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n116: \n117: | ID | Requirement |\n118: |----|-------------|\n119: | REQ-001 | A refusal after the name, a command named as a document, a wrapper in the wider set and a doc path beside a led refusal each read as a mention, and every request fixture still reads as a request |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":80}"},"time":{"start":1794865612218,"end":1794865612745}}}}
