{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865642136,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e65438ab001rS2FqlQefHMuV7","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e653ce2d001twlgWYgjaviJ5l","type":"tool","id":"call_b47d42ef9dda4290a6c2209e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":100,"offset":119,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md, lines 119-202\n119: | REQ-001 | A refusal after the name, a command named as a document, a wrapper in the wider set and a doc path beside a led refusal each read as a mention, and every request fixture still reads as a request |\n120: | REQ-002 | The suite reports 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, `FLOOR` prints 24/44, 0/35 and 2/44, `EVAL` prints [160,49,21,5] or better and the stored sets are unchanged |\n121: \n122: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n123: \n124: | ID | Requirement |\n125: |----|-------------|\n126: | REQ-003 | The playbook scenario's third prompt tops `/doctor:update` through the Claude hook |\n127: | REQ-004 | The four probe prompts top system-skill-advisor through `run-probes.cjs` |\n128: | REQ-005 | Review pass thirteen converges and the full alignment run reports 0 P0 and 0 P1, or each remaining one is recorded with the operator's decision |\n129: \n130: > Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n131: > which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n132: <!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n133: \n134: ---\n135: \n136: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n137: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n138: \n139: - **SC-001**: each new case fails on `b8ebee37d75` and passes after the fix\n140: - **SC-002**: the floors and stored sets are unchanged\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n146: ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n147: \n148: | Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n149: |------|------|--------|------------|\n150: | Risk | A tail refusal clause reads a real request as a refusal | High | REQUEST6, CONTROL5 and the wrapper matrix must stay requests |\n151: | Risk | New advisor phrases pull other prompts to the advisor | Medium | `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and the holdout count gate each phrase |\n152: | Risk | A fresh alignment run writes fresh probes | Medium | REQ-005 records any remainder with the operator's decision |\n153: <!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: <!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->\n158: ## L2: NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n159: <!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->\n160: \n161: ### Performance\n162: - **NFR-P01**: The fold adds a constant number of regex passes per prompt\n163: \n164: ### Security\n165: - **NFR-S01**: No holdout or command prompt text is read or printed\n166: - **NFR-S02**: `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` is never read or created\n167: \n168: ### Reliability\n169: - **NFR-R01**: Earlier phases' committed evidence stays unchanged\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: <!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n174: ## L2: EDGE CASES\n175: \n176: - Empty input: a prompt with no command name returns no mention\n177: - Maximum input: an or-list of wrapped commands with a refusal after the last one reads as a refusal of each\n178: - Failure path: \"run /speckit:save, don't skip it\" stays a request, because \"skip\" is not a use verb\n179: <!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n180: \n181: ---\n182: \n183: <!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n184: ## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n185: \n186: | Dimension | Score | Notes |\n187: |-----------|-------|-------|\n188: | Scope | 8/25 | One module, one test file, one playbook, one metadata file |\n189: | Risk | 11/25 | Command offers on every runtime |\n190: | Research | 4/20 | Each finding names its case |\n191: | **Total** | **23/70** | **Level 2** |\n192: <!-- /ANCHOR:complexity -->\n193: \