9-acceptance\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n164:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-traceability-tasks\", \"source\": \"d-traceability\", \"target\": \"file-039-tasks\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n165:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-in-dim-001\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\"},\n166:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-in-dim-002\", \"source\": \"f-002\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\"},\n167:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-in-file-001\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\"},\n168:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-in-file-002\", \"source\": \"f-002\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\"},\n169:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-evidence-001\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\"},\n170:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-evidence-002\", \"source\": \"ev-002\", \"target\": \"f-002\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\"}\n171:   ]\n172: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/iter-001.record.json, lines 1-172\n1: {\n2:   \"type\": \"iteration\",\n3:   \"iteration\": 1,\n4:   \"run\": 1,\n5:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n6:   \"target_agent\": \"deep-review\",\n7:   \"agent_definition_loaded\": true,\n8:   \"resolved_route\": \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\n9:   \"status\": \"complete\",\n10:   \"focus\": \"correctness and traceability - commandOnlyMentioned normalization and the wrapper invariance test\",\n11:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"traceability\"],\n12:   \"filesReviewed\": [\n13:     \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-549\",\n14:     \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:410-459\",\n15:     \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-573\",\n16:     \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:169-232\",\n17:     \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1200-1260\",\n18:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-12.txt:1-10\",\n19:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-12.txt:1-7\",\n20:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md:1-31\",\n21:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-10.md:1-28\",\n22:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md:60\",\n23:     \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md:64-65\"\n24:   ],\n25:   \"findingsCount\": 2,\n26:   \"findingsSummary\": {\"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1},\n27:   \"findingsNew\": {\"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1},\n28:   \"findingDetails\": [\n29:     {\n30:       \"id\": \"F001\",\n31:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n32:       \"title\": \"A markdown wrapper the normalizer does not strip turns a refusal or question into an offer\",\n33:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n34:       \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:427\",\n35:       \"evidence\": \"The strip chain drops backticks, asterisks, double quotes and only opening or closing single quotes, while COMMAND_GAP_WORDS at line 363 admits only plain words and apostrophes between a lead and the name. A bracketed, parenthesized, struck-through, HTML-tagged, guillemet or linked command keeps punctuation that blocks the anchored lead test at lines 444-450, so commandOnlyMentioned returns false and attachCommand offers the mutating command. Verified on all 12 refusal/question fixture rows across six wrapper pairs (72/72 flip) with 0 mismatches for the six covered pairs.\",\n36:       \"disposition\": \"active\",\n37:       \"findingClass\": \"algorithmic\",\n38:       \"scopeProof\": \"Ran the module's exported function over the 23 PLAIN_ROWS cross six non-normalized wrapper pairs: 72/72 refusal-question rows flipped, 0 request rows flipped, 0 mismatches for the six WRAPPERS pairs. The occurrence scan still finds the name inside the markup, so the failure is the lead match.\",\n39:       \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\n40:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\n41:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\",\n42:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\"\n43:       ],\n44:       \"recommendation\": \"Strip the markup wrappers the same way the existing marks are stripped, or let the lead gap ignore a short run of markup punctuation; extend WRAPPERS with the markdown set so the invariance test pins the whole class.\"\n45:     },\n46:     {\n47:       \"id\": \"F002\",\n48:       \"severity\": \"P2\",\n49:       \"title\": \"A doc-path mention of the command defeats a led refusal\",\n50:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n51:       \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:437\",\n52:       \"evidence\": \"The after-name lookahead blocks only [a-z0-9_-], unlike typedCommandIn's dot-and-slash continuation rule at line 234, so /create:readme.md and /create:readme/notes.txt count as occurrences. Every occurrence must carry a lead at line 439, so a led refusal plus an unled path reference returns false and attachCommand offers /create:readme.\",\n53:       \"disposition\": \"active\",\n54:       \"findingClass\": \"algorithmic\",\n55:       \"scopeProof\": \"The occurrence regex matches the name inside a .md file name and a directory segment; typedCommandIn already refuses both forms, so the two readers of the same prompt disagree on what a path is.\",\n56:       \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\n57:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\n58:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\"\n59:       ],\n60:       \"recommendation\": \"Apply the same dot-and-slash continuation rule after the name that typedCommandIn uses, or skip an occurrence whose following characters make it a path.\"\n61:     }\n62:   ],\n63:   \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n64:     \"results\": [\n65:       {\n66:         \"protocolId\": \"spec_code\",\n67:         \"status\": \"pass\",\n68:         \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n69:         \"applicable\": true,\n70:         \"evidence\": [\n71:           \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md:16-17\",\n72:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:427\"\n73:         ],\n74:         \"summary\": \"The branch diff is the two scope files and does what pass eleven's report says; F001 and F002 are new defects outside AC-007's enumerated marks.\"\n75:       },\n76:       {\n77:         \"protocolId\": \"checklist_evidence\",\n78:         \"status\": \"notApplicable\",\n79:         \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n80:         \"applicable\": false,\n81:         \"evidence\": [\n82:           \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md:60\"\n83:         ],\n84:         \"summary\": \"No packet checklist belongs to this review pass; 039 AC-007 was read as the wrapper contract and is met as written.\"\n85:       },\n86:       {\n87:         \"protocolId\": \"skill_agent\",\n88:         \"status\": \"pass\",\n89:         \"gateClass\": \"overlay\",\n90:         \"applicable\": true,\n91:         \"evidence\": [\n92:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-13\"\n93:         ],\n94:         \"summary\": \"No agent definition is in the diff; both changed files are runtime library and test files.\"\n95:       },\n96:       {\n97:         \"protocolId\": \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n98:         \"status\": \"notApplicable\",\n99:         \"gateClass\": \"overlay\",\n100:         \"applicable\": false,\n101:         \"evidence\": [\n102:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-10\"\n103:         ],\n104:         \"summary\": \"No runtime mirror is touched by the scope files.\"\n105:       },\n106:       {\n107:         \"protocolId\": \"feature_catalog_code\",\n108:         \"status\": \"partial\",\n109:         \"gateClass\": \"overlay\",\n110:         \"applicable\": true,\n111:         \"evidence\": [\n112:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:175-188\",\n113:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:232-234\"\n114:         ],\n115:         \"summary\": \"The wrapper test pins the six listed marks and the retired-name mapping; F001 names the wrapper class it cannot see, F002 the occurrence-boundary disagreement with typedCommandIn.\"\n116:       },\n117:       {\n118:         \"protocolId\": \"playbook_capability\",\n119:         \"status\": \"partial\",\n120:         \"gateClass\": \"overlay\",\n121:         \"applicable\": true,\n122:         \"evidence\": [\n123:           \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:42-73\"\n124:         ],\n125:         \"summary\": \"No playbook scenario was executed; the node module was exercised directly with the fixture rows and the uncovered wrapper pairs.\"\n126:       }\n127:     ]\n128:   },\n129:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 1.0,\n130:   \"noveltyJustification\": \"Both findings are first-time (no prior iteration exists). F001 comes from running the exported mention guard over the test's own fixture rows with six wrapper pairs the test does not list; F002 comes from the occurrence boundary matching a doc-path reference that typedCommandIn already refuses. Neither repeats a recorded pass-ten or pass-eleven finding.\",\n131:   \"sessionId\": \"fanout-mention-12-1794856957949-n58dw7\",\n132:   \"generation\": 1,\n133:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n134:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T19:37:36Z\",\n135:   \"durationMs\": 98000,\n136:   \"graphEvents\": [\n137:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"kind\": \"DIMENSION\", \"label\": \"correctness\"},\n138:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"d-traceability\", \"kind\": \"DIMENSION\", \"label\": \"traceability\"},\n139:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-command-attach\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\"},\n140:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-command-attach-guards\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\"},\n141:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-fusion\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\"},\n142:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-review-brief-12\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"review/review-brief-12.txt\"},\n143:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-review-scope-12\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"review/review-scope-12.txt\"},\n144:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-review-report\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"review/review-report.md\"},\n145:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-review-report-pass-10\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"review/review-report-pass-10.md\"},\n146:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-039-acceptance\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/acceptance-criteria.md\"},\n147:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"file-039-tasks\", \"kind\": \"FILE\", \"label\": \"039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md\"},\n148:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"kind\": \"FINDING\", \"label\": \"Unnormalized markdown wrapper turns a refusal into an offer\"},\n149:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"f-002\", \"kind\": \"FINDING\", \"label\": \"Doc-path occurrence defeats a led refusal\"},\n150:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"kind\": \"EVIDENCE\", \"label\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:427\"},\n151:     {\"type\": \"node\", \"id\": \"ev-002\", \"kind\": \"EVIDENCE\", \"label\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:437\"},\n152:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-correctness-attach\", \"source\": \"d-correctness\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n153:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-correctness-guards\", \"source\": \"d-correctness\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach-guards\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n154:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-correctness-fusion\", \"source\": \"d-correctness\", \"target\": \"file-fusion\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n155:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-correctness-brief\", \"source\": \"d-correctness\", \"target\": \"file-review-brief-12\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n156:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-correctness-scope\", \"source\": \"d-correctness\", \"target\": \"file-review-scope-12\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n157:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-traceability-attach\", \"source\": \"d-traceability\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n158:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-traceability-guards\", \"source\": \"d-traceability\", \"target\": \"file-command-attach-guards\", \"relation\": \"COVERS\"},\n159:     {\"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e1-cov-traceability-brief\", \"source\": \"d-traceabil