{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865918575,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6582e6a0015Vx5UCyxzKp8J3","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e6581bbf001Ly4UjW9wfLgXMI","type":"tool","id":"call_ee821a642e8140769745db50","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - command mention pass thirteen\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the mention-13 lineage, tracking the commandOnlyMentioned fold and tail-rule widening plus the typedCommandIn start boundary, with the guards test that pins them.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - mention-13\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent state for the `mention-13` lineage of review pass thirteen. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of the mention area for command surfacing pass thirteen: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. The area covers `commandOnlyMentioned`, which now drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, skips a doc-path occurrence, reads a refusal of `it` after the name, and reads a command named as a document after the, this or that; and `typedCommandIn`, whose start boundary now takes the same marks.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Reviewing the `data` area (graph-metadata.json intent phrases, the playbook prompt change, ADR-001) assigned to `data-13`; read-only context only.\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-13.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n- Re-reporting the open P2 of review passes ten to twelve or the `038-alignment-p1-remediation` P2 list.\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n- A blocked stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- None yet.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness. - Focus area: the two new tail rules (`COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN`, `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT`) and the widened occurrence boundary, probed against request wording. - Reason: init has no findings yet, and correctness is the risk the packet names as High. - Rotation status: first pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: none. - Required evidence: exported-function probes with concrete prompts plus file:line citations. - Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `command-attach.ts` `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY` (line 208), `typedCommandIn` (line 221), `COMMAND_USE_VERB`/`COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` (lines 362-363), `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` (line 374), `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` (line 392), `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 407), `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 413), `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` (line 419), `commandOnlyMentioned` (line 437), `attachCommand` (line 495), `typedCommandForTop` (line 256); `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` `WRAPPERS`/`PLAIN_ROWS` (lines 175-182), the later-refusal and document rows (lines 200-230), the typed wrapper rows (lines 518-525).\n- Behavior claims: a refused or questioned command is never offered; a request still is; the four new shapes read as mentions; a doc path is a file, not a naming; the typed reader starts on the same marks the fold drops.\n- Prior fixes: pass twelve dropped a quote opening a name and read a retired name in the mention check; this pass adds brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, the tail refusal, the document noun and the doc-path skip.\n- Consumers: `attachCommand` line 527 (hub routes), `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1204-1215` (`withholdMentionedCommands`), `typedCommandForTop` line 256.\n- Review risks: the two new tail rules run before the existing pronoun-request rule, so a later request can be shadowed; the tail refusal reads a negative clause without bounding what follows `it`; the occurrence lookahead now suppresses a name followed by `.` or `/`; the determiner requirement narrows the document rule that spec.md §3 states without it.\n- Out of scope: the `data` area, the scorer weights, the fidelity corpora and the broad routing accuracy suite; context only.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | - | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | - | - | 0 | pending |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-16T21:51:12Z\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - command mention pass thirteen\\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the mention-13 lineage, tracking the commandOnlyMentioned fold and tail-rule widening plus the typedCommandIn start boundary, with the guards test that pins them.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - mention-13\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent state for the `mention-13` lineage of review pass thirteen. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview of the mention area for command surfacing pass thirteen: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. The area covers `commandOnlyMentioned`, which now drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, skips a doc-path occurrence, reads a refusal of `it` after the name, and reads a command named as a document after the, this or that; and `typedCommandIn`, whose start boundary now takes the same marks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Reviewing the `data` area (graph-metadata.json intent phrases, the playbook prompt change, ADR-001) assigned to `data-13`; read-only context only.\\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-13.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\\n- Re-reporting the open P2 of review passes ten to twelve or the `038-alignment-p1-remediation` P2 list.\\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\\n- A blocked stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\\n- P1 (Required): 0\\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\\n- Resolved: 0\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- None yet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: correctness. - Focus area: the two new tail rules (`COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN`, `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT`) and the widened occurrence boundary, probed against request wording. - Reason: init has no findings yet, and correctness is the risk the packet names as High. - Rotation status: first pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: none. - Required evidence: exported-function probes with concrete prompts plus file:line citations. - Recovery note: none.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `command-attach.ts` `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY` (line 208), `typedCommandIn` (line 221), `COMMAND_USE_VERB`/`COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` (lines 362-363), `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` (line 374), `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` (line 392), `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 407), `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 413), `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` (line 419), `commandOnlyMentioned` (line 437), `attachCommand` (line 495), `typedCommandForTop` (line 256); `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` `WRAPPERS`/`PLAIN_ROWS` (lines 175-182), the later-refusal and document rows (lines 200-230), the typed wrapper rows (lines 518-525).\\n- Behavior claims: a refused or questioned command is never offered; a request still is; the four new shapes read as mentions; a doc path is a file, not a naming; the typed reader starts on the same marks the fold drops.\\n- Prior fixes: pass twelve dropped a quote opening a name and read a retired name in the mention check; this pass adds brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, the tail refusal, the document noun and the doc-path skip.\\n- Consumers: `attachCommand` line 527 (hub routes), `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1204-1215` (`withholdMentionedCommands`), `typedCommandForTop` line 256.\\n- Review risks: the two new tail rules run before the existing pronoun-request rule, so a later request can be shadowed; the tail refusal reads a negative clause without bounding what follows `it`; the occurrence lookahead now suppresses a name followed by `.` or `/`; the determiner requirement narrows the document rule that spec.md §3 states without it.\\n- Out of scope: the `data` area, the scorer weights, the fidelity corpora and the broad routing accuracy suite; context only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | - | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | - | - | 0 | pending |\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-16T21:51:12Z\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794865901162,"end":1794865918575}}}}
