{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794866207475,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e65cc9c8001EXYeHvqfGwUgho","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e65cbc37001OMaLbo4nEhxOLA","type":"tool","id":"call_460c02c1fb11430db9dda312","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\n- Iteration 1: running the exported guards over concrete prompts instead of only reading the new test rows. It produced F001 and F002 in one pass, and both are prompts the suite cannot see because its fixture rows carry no document naming and no limiting clause.\n- Iteration 1: re-running the unchanged `REFUSE8`, `QUESTION2`, `REQUEST6` and `CONTROL5` rows on the current tree first. That baseline kept the two P1s honest: the branch does not regress the pinned fixtures, so the findings are new shapes rather than a broken suite.\n- Iteration 1: testing the tail regex against the old decision path. The pronoun-request regex matches the F001 tail, which proves the new early return is what changes the reading rather than a pre-existing gap.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n- Iteration 1: the first probe set assumed a determiner plus `command` would capture `run the /deep:review command on this packet`. It does not, because `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` needs a document noun after `command`. The probe was corrected to the document-noun forms before any finding was written.\n- Iteration 1: `spec.md:72` looked like a stale claim until the surrounding block was read; it is pre-fix evidence for the bracket defect this branch closes, so no finding was raised."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -67,14 +67,19 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\n+- Iteration 1: running the exported guards over concrete prompts instead of only reading the new test rows. It produced F001 and F002 in one pass, and both are prompts the suite cannot see because its fixture rows carry no document naming and no limiting clause.\n+- Iteration 1: re-running the unchanged `REFUSE8`, `QUESTION2`, `REQUEST6` and `CONTROL5` rows on the current tree first. That baseline kept the two P1s honest: the branch does not regress the pinned fixtures, so the findings are new shapes rather than a broken suite.\n+- Iteration 1: testing the tail regex against the old decision path. The pronoun-request regex matches the F001 tail, which proves the new early return is what changes the reading rather than a pre-existing gap.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Init: none.\n+- Iteration 1: the first probe set assumed a determiner plus `command` would capture `run the /deep:review command on this packet`. It does not, because `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` needs a document noun after `command`. The probe was corrected to the document-noun forms before any finding was written.\n+- Iteration 1: `spec.md:72` looked like a stale claim until the surrounding block was read; it is pre-fix evidence for the bracket defect this branch closes, so no finding was raised.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file and both scope files before choosing a focus; the acknowledgement block names this lineage's area by label.\\n- Iteration 1: running the exported guards over concrete prompts instead of only reading the new test rows. It produced F001 and F002 in one pass, and both are prompts the suite cannot see because its fixture rows carry no document naming and no limiting clause.\\n- Iteration 1: re-running the unchanged `REFUSE8`, `QUESTION2`, `REQUEST6` and `CONTROL5` rows on the current tree first. That baseline kept the two P1s honest: the branch does not regress the pinned fixtures, so the findings are new shapes rather than a broken suite.\\n- Iteration 1: testing the tail regex against the old decision path. The pronoun-request regex matches the F001 tail, which proves the new early return is what changes the reading rather than a pre-existing gap.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\\n- Iteration 1: the first probe set assumed a determiner plus `command` would capture `run the /deep:review command on this packet`. It does not, because `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` needs a document noun after `command`. The probe was corrected to the document-noun forms before any finding was written.\\n- Iteration 1: `spec.md:72` looked like a stale claim until the surrounding block was read; it is pre-fix evidence for the bracket defect this branch closes, so no finding was raised.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794866203080,"end":1794866207475}}}}
