urfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:131',\\n      evidence: 'tasks.md:131 states \\\"Every wrapper and lead in the mention check is covered by the invariance matrix\\\". The matrix at command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:179-189 runs PLAIN_ROWS only, and PLAIN_ROWS holds REFUSE8, QUESTION2, REQUEST6, CONTROL5 and two or-list rows; COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN and COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT appear only in the unwrapped it.each blocks at lines 202-230. Probed wrapped forms: \\\"[/create:readme] is not what I want, do not run it\\\" and \\\"read the “/create:readme” document\\\" both still read as mentions, so behaviour holds and the claim is what is wrong.',\\n      disposition: 'active', findingClass: 'evidence-overstatement',\\n      scopeProof: 'Read PLAIN_ROWS and both new it.each blocks; the new rows are outside the matrix input set. Ran the wrapped document naming and the wrapped tail refusal through the guard; both classify correctly.',\\n      affectedSurfaceHints: ['specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md', '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts'],\\n      recommendation: 'Add the two new rows to PLAIN_ROWS so the matrix covers the new leads, or narrow the checklist sentence to the leads the matrix runs.'\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  traceabilityChecks: {\\n    results: [\\n      { protocolId: 'spec_code', status: 'partial', gateClass: 'hard', applicable: true, evidence: ['specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:85', 'specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:86-87', '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:440-451'], summary: 'The document bullet is narrower in code (F005); the fold and doc-path bullets match.' },\\n      { protocolId: 'checklist_evidence', status: 'partial', gateClass: 'hard', app