{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794866702191,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6643e2b001w0pRhnACVOFhxi","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e6642f070012H3WT0pJDH70Nl","type":"tool","id":"call_487c29b937d345ea97d308ea","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13 && python3 - \"$L/deep-review-strategy.md\" <<'PY'\nimport sys\np = sys.argv[1]\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- Iteration 2: checking the checklist sentence against the matrix's input set rather than its description. That is what separated F006 from a behaviour finding, and a wrapped probe confirmed the behaviour holds.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Iteration 2: checking the checklist sentence against the matrix's input set rather than its description. That is what separated F006 from a behaviour finding, and a wrapped probe confirmed the behaviour holds.\n- Iteration 3: reading the whole module for import, environment and filesystem access instead of scanning one region. An empty scan is decisive for a clean security result, and it is cheaper than arguing the boundary.\n- Iteration 3: measuring the new patterns at size (1.56 ms at 100 KB, 2.08 ms on a 68 KB repeated negation, 2.62 ms on 2,000 unled occurrences) rather than asserting a cost.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- Iteration 2: AC-002's suite-wide claim cannot be re-run from this lineage, which runs no suite and writes no test output; it stays unverified and is recorded as a missing dependency rather than assumed.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Iteration 2: AC-002's suite-wide claim cannot be re-run from this lineage, which runs no suite and writes no test output; it stays unverified and is recorded as a missing dependency rather than assumed.\n- Iteration 3: the iteration record first carried `findingsCount: 0` with the running summary `P1: 2, P2: 4`. The reducer read that as six per-run counts and padded six summary-only findings, which then failed the evidence-density gate. The repair is recorded: the record was re-issued with `findingsCount: 6` so the summary reads as cumulative, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line was rewritten to that corrected record so the delta and the log agree. That is the one write-once file this lineage rewrote, and it changed only the count fields.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `spec_code` | core | partial | 2 | The four refusal shapes and the wider fold match `spec.md:57,86`; the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). |\",\n              \"| `spec_code` | core | partial | 3 | The four refusal shapes and the wider fold match `spec.md:57,86`; the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 2 | AC-001's five prompts read as mentions and REQUEST6/CONTROL5 stay requests; `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006). |\",\n              \"| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 3 | AC-001's five prompts read as mentions and REQUEST6/CONTROL5 stay requests; `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006); NFR-P01 holds. |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 1 | No agent definition is in the diff. |\",\n              \"| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 3 | No agent definition is in the diff. |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No runtime mirror is touched by the two scope files. |\",\n              \"| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | No runtime mirror is touched by the two scope files. |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 2 | The matrix pins the twelve wrapper pairs; F001, F002 and F006 are the shapes the plan's verification cannot see. |\",\n              \"| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 3 | The matrix pins the twelve wrapper pairs; F001, F002 and F006 are the shapes the plan's verification cannot see. |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | The playbook row in this pass belongs to the data area; no mention-area scenario exists. |\",\n              \"| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | The playbook row in this pass belongs to the data area; no mention-area scenario exists for a security property. |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 2 P1, 3 P2 | partial |\",\n              \"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 3 | 2 P1, 3 P2 | partial |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 1 P2 | partial |\",\n              \"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 3 | 1 P2 | partial |\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- AC-004 as a mention-area regression: the waiver belongs to `ADR-001` and the data area (iteration 2).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- AC-004 as a mention-area regression: the waiver belongs to `ADR-001` and the data area (iteration 2).\n- A prompt-controlled regex or secret surface: the module has no import, environment, filesystem or network access, and names reach the regex only through `escapePhrase` (iteration 3).\n- ReDoS in the two new patterns: fixed-literal alternations with no nested quantifier; 1.56 ms at 100 KB and 2.08 ms on a 68 KB repeated negation (iteration 3).\n- A homoglyph, zero-width or fullwidth bypass: an untracked form never matches `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, so no route selects a command (iteration 3).\n- A denial-of-service from the widened fold: six more dropped characters do not change the pass count (iteration 3).\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY"},"output":"ok\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13 && python3 - \\\"$L/deep-review-strategy.md\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport sys\\np = sys.argv[1]\\ns = open(p).read()\\ns = s.replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"- Iteration 2: checking the checklist sentence against the matrix's input set rather than its description. That is what separated F006 from a behaviour finding, and a wrapped probe confirmed the behaviour holds.\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"- Iteration 2: checking the checklist sentence against the matrix's input set rather than its description. That is what separated F006 from a behaviour finding, and a wrapped probe confirmed the behaviour holds.\\n- Iteration 3: reading the whole module for import, environment and filesystem access instead of scanning one region. An empty scan is decisive for a clean security result, and it is cheaper than arguing the boundary.\\n- Iteration 3: measuring the new patterns at size (1.56 ms at 100 KB, 2.08 ms on a 68 KB repeated negation, 2.62 ms on 2,000 unled occurrences) rather than asserting a cost.\\\"\\\"\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"- Iteration 2: AC-002's suite-wide claim cannot be re-run from this lineage, which runs no suite and writes no test output; it stays unverified and is recorded as a missing dependency rather than assumed.\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"- Iteration 2: AC-002's suite-wide claim cannot be re-run from this lineage, which runs no suite and writes no test output; it stays unverified and is recorded as a missing dependency rather than assumed.\\n- Iteration 3: the iteration record first carried `findingsCount: 0` with the running summary `P1: 2, P2: 4`. The reducer read that as six per-run counts and padded six summary-only findings, which then failed the evidence-density gate. The repair is recorded: the record was re-issued with `findingsCount: 6` so the summary reads as cumulative, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line was rewritten to that corrected record so the delta and the log agree. That is the one write-once file this lineage rewrote, and it changed only the count fields.\\\"\\\"\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `spec_code` | core | partial | 2 | The four refusal shapes and the wider fold match `spec.md:57,86`; the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `spec_code` | core | partial | 3 | The four refusal shapes and the wider fold match `spec.md:57,86`; the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 2 | AC-001's five prompts read as mentions and REQUEST6/CONTROL5 stay requests; `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006). |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 3 | AC-001's five prompts read as mentions and REQUEST6/CONTROL5 stay requests; `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006); NFR-P01 holds. |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 1 | No agent definition is in the diff. |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 3 | No agent definition is in the diff. |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No runtime mirror is touched by the two scope files. |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | No runtime mirror is touched by the two scope files. |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 2 | The matrix pins the twelve wrapper pairs; F001, F002 and F006 are the shapes the plan's verification cannot see. |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 3 | The matrix pins the twelve wrapper pairs; F001, F002 and F006 are the shapes the plan's verification cannot see. |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | The playbook row in this pass belongs to the data area; no mention-area scenario exists. |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | The playbook row in this pass belongs to the data area; no mention-area scenario exists for a security property. |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 2 P1, 3 P2 | partial |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 3 | 2 P1, 3 P2 | partial |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 1 P2 | partial |\\\",\\n              \\\"| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 3 | 1 P2 | partial |\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"- AC-004 as a mention-area regression: the waiver belongs to `ADR-001` and the data area (iteration 2).\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"- AC-004 as a mention-area regression: the waiver belongs to `ADR-001` and the data area (iteration 2).\\n- A prompt-controlled regex or secret surface: the module has no import, environment, filesystem or network access, and names reach the regex only through `escapePhrase` (iteration 3).\\n- ReDoS in the two new patterns: fixed-literal alternations with no nested quantifier; 1.56 ms at 100 KB and 2.08 ms on a 68 KB repeated negation (iteration 3).\\n- A homoglyph, zero-width or fullwidth bypass: an untracked form never matches `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, so no route selects a command (iteration 3).\\n- A denial-of-service from the widened fold: six more dropped characters do not change the pass count (iteration 3).\\\"\\\"\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nprint(\\\"ok\\\")\\nPY\"}"},"time":{"start":1794866691627,"end":1794866702191}}}}
