{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794866733731,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e664a955001HfpSWme020sr9y","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e6647e77001fsHGa52zmrQhin","type":"tool","id":"call_9c83ee4a47bf494785de3b8d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004 - mention-13\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review. Target agent: `@deep-review`, executed in-process by this detached fan-out lineage (no nested dispatch).\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`.\n- Iteration: 4 of 8. Dimension: maintainability. Focus: the comment paragraph the diff reflowed and the readability of the two new rules' documentation.\n- Operator review focus, and how this iteration addressed it: pass thirteen's brief asks for a request that now reads as a mention and for a refusal or question shape still read as a request. This iteration asked how cheaply the next reader can see which shape each rule covers: whether the fold's contract is stated readably and whether the new rules are documented where a maintainer will look. It found one reflow defect (F007) and otherwise clean documentation.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:409-476` (the two new rule comments, the fold comment, the function)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:197-245` (typed reader comment for comparison)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-232` (the comments on the new test rows)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. F001 and F002 remain active and are carried forward.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The fold comment was left mid-sentence by the reflow** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:435` -- the paragraph at lines 421-436 now ends with a 148-character line, a 48-character line, a 15-character line (`// maps to. The`) and a 57-character line (`// command reads as the plain refusal does. An underscore`), while every other line in the block runs 75 to 82 characters. The diff inserted the doc-path clause into the last sentence and re-wrapped only that part, so the sentence that carries the fold's whole contract now reads across two widths and a stranded `The`.\n   Finding class: documentation-readability\n   Scope proof: Measured every line of the block: 421-426 and 428-431 are 78 to 81 characters, 432 is 15, 435 is 148, 436 is 48. The block is the only place the fold's contract is written down, and `commandOnlyMentioned` has no other doc comment.\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\n   Case: a maintainer adding a sixth wrapper or a new tail rule reads lines 421-436 to learn what the fold guarantees, and the sentence naming the doc-path skip is the one the reflow broke.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). The scope bullet's fold claim still matches the characters dropped at lines 440-441. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006). The test comments at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-232` describe each new row's intent in the same style as the older rows. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition in scope for this dimension. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `plan.md:70` names the guards test and the matrix as the verification for the widened check; F001, F002 and F006 remain the shapes that verification cannot see. |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook scenario covers the mention guard's documentation. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\nNone this iteration: the maintainability pass read the module and its test comments only.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguity: whether a comment reflow is worth a finding at all. It is recorded at P2 because the block is the module's only statement of the fold's contract, and the reflow stranded a sentence boundary rather than only changing line lengths.\n- Contradiction: none.\n- Partial success: the module's own style has other long constant lines (413 and 419 are 127 and 127 characters), so line length alone is not the defect; the orphaned sentence fragments are. The finding states both.\n- Correction carried from iteration 3: the iteration 3 record was re-issued with `findingsCount: 6` so its summary reads as the running total, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line was rewritten to match. The reducer now reports six open findings, not twelve. This is disclosed here because it is the lineage's one write-once overwrite.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The two new rule comments state their contract and the case that would break them (`run /speckit:save and don't skip it` stays a request; a typed request puts its argument after the name), which is the pattern the module's other rules follow.\n- The test comments on the new rows name the intent of each block, and the wrapper matrix's own comment still explains why it exists.\n- The module header's \"kept free of imports\" claim still holds at lines 1-14.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A stale comment on the typed reader: the widened `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY` at line 208 is described by the fold comment at 425-427, and the typed reader's comment at 197-207 still describes its own rules correctly.\n- A missing doc comment on `commandOnlyMentioned`: the fold paragraph is its doc comment, so F007 is the right object rather than a missing-documentation finding.\n- A naming or ownership defect in the generated tables: untouched by this pass and outside the scope file's diff.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining. All four dimensions are covered and the six findings are re-verified; the stop decision is the only open question.\n- Focus area: none.\n- Reason: four iterations covered correctness, traceability, security and maintainability, and the two active P1s are unchanged.\n- Rotation status: exhausted.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive `exported-function probes with concrete prompts` for a follow-up pass after fixes.\n- Required evidence: the convergence script's stop decision, recorded in the state log.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004 - mention-13\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review. Target agent: `@deep-review`, executed in-process by this detached fan-out lineage (no nested dispatch).\\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`.\\n- Iteration: 4 of 8. Dimension: maintainability. Focus: the comment paragraph the diff reflowed and the readability of the two new rules' documentation.\\n- Operator review focus, and how this iteration addressed it: pass thirteen's brief asks for a request that now reads as a mention and for a refusal or question shape still read as a request. This iteration asked how cheaply the next reader can see which shape each rule covers: whether the fold's contract is stated readably and whether the new rules are documented where a maintainer will look. It found one reflow defect (F007) and otherwise clean documentation.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:409-476` (the two new rule comments, the fold comment, the function)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:197-245` (typed reader comment for comparison)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-232` (the comments on the new test rows)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F001 and F002 remain active and are carried forward.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The fold comment was left mid-sentence by the reflow** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:435` -- the paragraph at lines 421-436 now ends with a 148-character line, a 48-character line, a 15-character line (`// maps to. The`) and a 57-character line (`// command reads as the plain refusal does. An underscore`), while every other line in the block runs 75 to 82 characters. The diff inserted the doc-path clause into the last sentence and re-wrapped only that part, so the sentence that carries the fold's whole contract now reads across two widths and a stranded `The`.\\n   Finding class: documentation-readability\\n   Scope proof: Measured every line of the block: 421-426 and 428-431 are 78 to 81 characters, 432 is 15, 435 is 148, 436 is 48. The block is the only place the fold's contract is written down, and `commandOnlyMentioned` has no other doc comment.\\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\\n   Case: a maintainer adding a sixth wrapper or a new tail rule reads lines 421-436 to learn what the fold guarantees, and the sentence naming the doc-path skip is the one the reflow broke.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: the document bullet is narrower in code (F005). The scope bullet's fold claim still matches the characters dropped at lines 440-441. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: `CHK-FIX-002` overstates matrix coverage (F006). The test comments at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-232` describe each new row's intent in the same style as the older rows. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition in scope for this dimension. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `plan.md:70` names the guards test and the matrix as the verification for the widened check; F001, F002 and F006 remain the shapes that verification cannot see. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook scenario covers the mention guard's documentation. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\nNone this iteration: the maintainability pass read the module and its test comments only.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguity: whether a comment reflow is worth a finding at all. It is recorded at P2 because the block is the module's only statement of the fold's contract, and the reflow stranded a sentence boundary rather than only changing line lengths.\\n- Contradiction: none.\\n- Partial success: the module's own style has other long constant lines (413 and 419 are 127 and 127 characters), so line length alone is not the defect; the orphaned sentence fragments are. The finding states both.\\n- Correction carried from iteration 3: the iteration 3 record was re-issued with `findingsCount: 6` so its summary reads as the running total, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line was rewritten to match. The reducer now reports six open findings, not twelve. This is disclosed here because it is the lineage's one write-once overwrite.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The two new rule comments state their contract and the case that would break them (`run /speckit:save and don't skip it` stays a request; a typed request puts its argument after the name), which is the pattern the module's other rules follow.\\n- The test comments on the new rows name the intent of each block, and the wrapper matrix's own comment still explains why it exists.\\n- The module header's \\\"kept free of imports\\\" claim still holds at lines 1-14.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A stale comment on the typed reader: the widened `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY` at line 208 is described by the fold comment at 425-427, and the typed reader's comment at 197-207 still describes its own rules correctly.\\n- A missing doc comment on `commandOnlyMentioned`: the fold paragraph is its doc comment, so F007 is the right object rather than a missing-documentation finding.\\n- A naming or ownership defect in the generated tables: untouched by this pass and outside the scope file's diff.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining. All four dimensions are covered and the six findings are re-verified; the stop decision is the only open question.\\n- Focus area: none.\\n- Reason: four iterations covered correctness, traceability, security and maintainability, and the two active P1s are unchanged.\\n- Rotation status: exhausted.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive `exported-function probes with concrete prompts` for a follow-up pass after fixes.\\n- Required evidence: the convergence script's stop decision, recorded in the state log.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794866719061,"end":1794866733731}}}}
