{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794867050614,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e669833c002UvvDOlC5wYY07W","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e6696c590010iQposocLJndWg","type":"tool","id":"call_b3ed6b57d01c4a8b88fc9eaf","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 007 - mention-13\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review. Target agent: `@deep-review`, executed in-process by this detached fan-out lineage (no nested dispatch).\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`.\n- Iteration: 7 of 8. Dimension: security (recovery pass, line-level granularity). The stop decision at iteration 6 was `STUCK_RECOVERY` / `stuckThresholdReached` after two no-progress passes, so this pass changes granularity rather than repeating the dimension sweep: every mark in the fold and in the typed start boundary is probed on its own, and the two readers are compared mark by mark.\n- Operator review focus, and how this iteration addressed it: pass thirteen's brief asks for a request that now reads as a mention and for a refusal still read as a request. At mark-level granularity the two failure directions become \"the typed reader accepts a mark the mention scan does not see\" and \"a refusal wrapped in a mark still offers the command\". Both were probed for thirteen wrapper pairs and nine single marks; neither fails.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:208` (typed start boundary)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:440-441` (fold)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:449-476` (occurrence scan and the tail rules)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:175-189,518-525` (the matrix and typed rows)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. F001 and F002 remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | F005 stands. The fold's mark set at 440-441 matches `spec.md:86` mark for mark. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | F006 stands. The matrix's twelve pairs at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:175-178` are the same twelve probed here, plus the ninth pair added by the row for prime and single-guillemet forms. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition in scope. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature catalog update in this pass. |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook scenario covers the mention guard. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n`typedCommandIn` at line 221 and `commandOnlyMentioned` at line 437 agree on every mark probed, so a wrapper cannot make a refusal reach `typedCommandForTop` as a typed command while the guard reads it as something else.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Recovery activation: the stop decision at iteration 6 named `stuckThresholdReached`, and the recovery row records `change-granularity-line-level` with `security` as the target dimension. This iteration is that pass; it is not a repeat of iteration 3's whole-file scan.\n- Ambiguity: whether a mark accepted by neither reader is a defect. It is not: an unrecognized mark leaves the command plainly typed or plainly refused, which is the pre-existing behaviour for every character outside the set.\n- Partial success: the coverage gate stays blocked by the two partial core protocols, as in iterations 5 and 6.\n- Contradiction: none.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Thirteen wrapper pairs (`backtick`, straight single, straight double, curly double, curly single, bold, brackets, parentheses, strikethrough, `<code>`, guillemets, prime, single guillemets) all satisfy three conditions at once: `typedCommandIn` finds `/deep:review`, the same wrapped form in a refusal reads as a mention, and the same wrapped form in a request reads as a request. 0 mismatches.\n- Nine single marks (`]`, `)`, `>`, `*`, `~`, `[`, `(`, `«`, `′`) appended to a typed command still leave it a typed command, and the same form in a refusal still reads as a mention.\n- The occurrence scan's prefix class `(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])` at line 451 is wider than the typed start boundary at line 208, so any typed hit is also an occurrence and the guard cannot miss a naming the typed reader found.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A divergence between the two readers' mark sets: the occurrence prefix is wider than the typed boundary, and all thirteen pairs agree in both directions.\n- A mark that hides a refusal from the typed path: `typedCommandForTop` calls the mention guard first, so a refusal still wins for the same wrapped form.\n- A regression introduced by the recovery pass's narrower probes: no code was modified, and every probe reads current bytes.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: cross-reference final pass. All four dimensions are covered; the next pass verifies that the artifact set agrees with itself before the cap stop.\n- Focus area: iteration files, deltas, state log rows and the registry.\n- Reason: the iteration cap is reached next, so the last pass should leave the lineage internally consistent rather than open a new direction.\n- Rotation status: re-verification pass 3 of 4 under the cap; the cap stop is expected at iteration 8.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive `probe both readers on the same input` for any future wrapper change.\n- Required evidence: file existence, record counts and registry counts.\n- Recovery note: the stuck recovery is spent; the cap stop is the terminal path.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 007 - mention-13\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review. Target agent: `@deep-review`, executed in-process by this detached fan-out lineage (no nested dispatch).\\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`.\\n- Iteration: 7 of 8. Dimension: security (recovery pass, line-level granularity). The stop decision at iteration 6 was `STUCK_RECOVERY` / `stuckThresholdReached` after two no-progress passes, so this pass changes granularity rather than repeating the dimension sweep: every mark in the fold and in the typed start boundary is probed on its own, and the two readers are compared mark by mark.\\n- Operator review focus, and how this iteration addressed it: pass thirteen's brief asks for a request that now reads as a mention and for a refusal still read as a request. At mark-level granularity the two failure directions become \\\"the typed reader accepts a mark the mention scan does not see\\\" and \\\"a refusal wrapped in a mark still offers the command\\\". Both were probed for thirteen wrapper pairs and nine single marks; neither fails.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:208` (typed start boundary)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:440-441` (fold)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:449-476` (occurrence scan and the tail rules)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:175-189,518-525` (the matrix and typed rows)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F001 and F002 remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | F005 stands. The fold's mark set at 440-441 matches `spec.md:86` mark for mark. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | F006 stands. The matrix's twelve pairs at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:175-178` are the same twelve probed here, plus the ninth pair added by the row for prime and single-guillemet forms. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition in scope. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature catalog update in this pass. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook scenario covers the mention guard. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n`typedCommandIn` at line 221 and `commandOnlyMentioned` at line 437 agree on every mark probed, so a wrapper cannot make a refusal reach `typedCommandForTop` as a typed command while the guard reads it as something else.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Recovery activation: the stop decision at iteration 6 named `stuckThresholdReached`, and the recovery row records `change-granularity-line-level` with `security` as the target dimension. This iteration is that pass; it is not a repeat of iteration 3's whole-file scan.\\n- Ambiguity: whether a mark accepted by neither reader is a defect. It is not: an unrecognized mark leaves the command plainly typed or plainly refused, which is the pre-existing behaviour for every character outside the set.\\n- Partial success: the coverage gate stays blocked by the two partial core protocols, as in iterations 5 and 6.\\n- Contradiction: none.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Thirteen wrapper pairs (`backtick`, straight single, straight double, curly double, curly single, bold, brackets, parentheses, strikethrough, `<code>`, guillemets, prime, single guillemets) all satisfy three conditions at once: `typedCommandIn` finds `/deep:review`, the same wrapped form in a refusal reads as a mention, and the same wrapped form in a request reads as a request. 0 mismatches.\\n- Nine single marks (`]`, `)`, `>`, `*`, `~`, `[`, `(`, `«`, `′`) appended to a typed command still leave it a typed command, and the same form in a refusal still reads as a mention.\\n- The occurrence scan's prefix class `(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])` at line 451 is wider than the typed start boundary at line 208, so any typed hit is also an occurrence and the guard cannot miss a naming the typed reader found.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A divergence between the two readers' mark sets: the occurrence prefix is wider than the typed boundary, and all thirteen pairs agree in both directions.\\n- A mark that hides a refusal from the typed path: `typedCommandForTop` calls the mention guard first, so a refusal still wins for the same wrapped form.\\n- A regression introduced by the recovery pass's narrower probes: no code was modified, and every probe reads current bytes.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: cross-reference final pass. All four dimensions are covered; the next pass verifies that the artifact set agrees with itself before the cap stop.\\n- Focus area: iteration files, deltas, state log rows and the registry.\\n- Reason: the iteration cap is reached next, so the last pass should leave the lineage internally consistent rather than open a new direction.\\n- Rotation status: re-verification pass 3 of 4 under the cap; the cap stop is expected at iteration 8.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive `probe both readers on the same input` for any future wrapper change.\\n- Required evidence: file existence, record counts and registry counts.\\n- Recovery note: the stuck recovery is spent; the cap stop is the terminal path.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794867036988,"end":1794867050614}}}}
