{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794867305315,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e66d018e001xLpOU0zgh46daV","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e66cd9da001kfbGk974AssBZR","type":"tool","id":"call_01d33495dcba47b68918d2c0","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - command mention pass thirteen (mention-13)\n\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), mention area\n- Scope files: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\n- Diff reviewed: `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437`\n- Iterations: 7 dispatched passes (8 iteration rows; run 3 was re-recorded), stop reason `maxIterationsReached`\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n**Overall verdict: FAIL.** The registry verdict is CONDITIONAL (0 P0, 2 P1, 5 P2), and the required coverage gate failed at the terminal stop (`traceability-incomplete`), which makes the session verdict FAIL under the review contract. No P0 was found; nothing here is an incident, and nothing here is a clean close either.\n\n`hasAdvisories: false` (the flag is only set on PASS).\n\nThe counts the verdict used: **P0 0, P1 2, P2 5**.\n\nWhat the two P1s say, in one line each:\n\n1. A command named as a document now reads as a mention even when the same prompt then asks to run it, so `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` loses the command the reader typed (F001).\n2. A limiting negation after the name now reads as a refusal, so `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` loses the command too (F002).\n\nBoth sit in the request direction the packet names as a High risk (`spec.md:150`), and both were introduced by this branch's two new tail rules. The five P2s are two more reader-shape gaps, one spec text wider than the code, one checklist claim wider than the matrix, and one reflowed comment.\n\nWhy the coverage gate failed: the two core traceability protocols stay `partial` because F005 (the spec bullet) and F006 (the checklist claim) are packet-text defects that a read-only lineage cannot repair. The loop therefore ran to the 8-iteration cap instead of converging, and the gate that stops a run from closing over an overstated checklist did its job.\n\nSelf-check outcomes: both P1s carry typed claim-adjudication packets and were confirmed, not downgraded. No P0 candidate arose, so no Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass was owed. F007 was narrowed in iteration 6 after `git show b8ebee37d75` showed two of the four comment lines it first blamed predate the branch.\n\nOperator review focus, verbatim: `Review pass thirteen. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.`\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` **is required**: two active P1 findings plus a failing required gate.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": {\n    \"P0\": 0,\n    \"P1\": 2,\n    \"P2\": 5,\n    \"ids\": [\"F001\", \"F002\", \"F003\", \"F004\", \"F005\", \"F006\", \"F007\"]\n  },\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-1\",\n      \"priority\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Keep a later request a request\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F001\", \"F002\"],\n      \"surface\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-2\",\n      \"priority\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Close the two reader-shape gaps\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F003\", \"F004\"],\n      \"surface\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-3\",\n      \"priority\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Align the packet text and checklist evidence with the code\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F005\", \"F006\"],\n      \"surface\": \"040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md, 040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-4\",\n      \"priority\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Re-wrap the fold comment\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F007\"],\n      \"surface\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Add the determiner condition to the document bullet in spec.md §3 and to REQ-001, or widen the code to accept an article-less doc naming.\",\n    \"Restate CHK-FIX-002 so it names the leads the invariance matrix actually runs, or move the two new rows into PLAIN_ROWS.\",\n    \"Record that a later request clause outranks a document naming, and that a qualified negation (`don't run it twice`) is a limit rather than a refusal.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add a failing-first test for `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` and for `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff`.\",\n    \"Add a failing-first test for `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget`.\",\n    \"Move the COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT return after the COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN check, or let the pronoun-request check win.\",\n    \"Bound COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN to a clause that ends at `it` or continues with a sentence boundary.\",\n    \"Drop the `](target)` pair (or treat `](` as a boundary) before the fold, so a markdown link label keeps its own occurrence.\",\n    \"Add the two new rows to PLAIN_ROWS, or narrow the CHK-FIX-002 sentence to the leads the matrix runs.\",\n    \"Re-wrap comment lines 421-436 to the block width.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"logic-ordering\", \"logic-overreach\", \"normalization-edge\", \"vocabulary-asymmetry\", \"spec-drift\", \"evidence-overstatement\", \"documentation-readability\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### P1 - Required\n\n**F001 - A document naming returns a mention before a later request clause is read**\n- Dimension: correctness. File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:458`.\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` returns `true` before the `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` check at line 460. The contract at lines 403-407 says a use-verb clause with `it` turns an earlier naming into a request.\n- Impact: `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` yields `typedCommandForTop(...) === undefined`; `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff` yields `attachCommand(...) === undefined` even though `thorough` matches `DEPTH_REQUEST`.\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: logic-ordering.\n- Scope proof: exported guards and consumer run on both prompts; both classify as mentions, and the unchanged pronoun regex matches the tail `command file, then run it`, so the earlier read was a request.\n- Affected surface hints: `command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\n- Fix: move the document return after the pronoun-request check, or let a use-verb clause win.\n\n**F002 - A limiting negation after the name reads as a refusal**\n- Dimension: correctness. File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413`.\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` ends at `it\\b`, so any qualifier after `it` still refuses.\n- Impact: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` lose the typed command.\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: logic-overreach.\n- Scope proof: both prompts classify as mentions; the unchanged lead tests cannot produce that reading, so `b8ebee37d75` returned a request.\n- Affected surface hints: `command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\n- Fix: bound the tail refusal at `it` or a sentence boundary.\n\n### P2 - Advisories\n\n**F003 - A markdown link label abuts its target and the naming stops being an occurrence** - `command-attach.ts:441` - the fold drops brackets and parentheses, so `[/create:readme](https://example.com/docs)` merges into `/create:readmehttps://...`, the lookahead at 451 rejects it and `occurrences.length === 0` returns `false`. `do not run [/create:readme](https://example.com/docs) yet` therefore offers `/create:readme`. Class: normalization-edge.\n\n**F004 - The post-name reader covers one clause shape** - `command-attach.ts:459` - a question (`/create:readme, what does it do?`) and a sibling refusal (`/create:readme is wrong, skip it`) still read as requests and offer the command. Class: vocabulary-asymmetry.\n\n**F005 - The spec's document bullet is wider than the code's determiner rule** - `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:85` - the bullet and `REQ-001` (`spec.md:119`) state the document shape without a determiner; the code requires `the|this|that` at `command-attach.ts:458`. `read /create:readme documentation and tell me what it does` still offers the command. `tasks.md:46` records the narrowing as deliberate, so the packet text is the stale part. Class: spec-drift.\n\n**F006 - CHK-FIX-002 claims matrix coverage for leads the matrix never wraps** - `040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:131` - `PLAIN_ROWS` (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:179-182`) holds only the older fixtures, while `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` and `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` appear only in the unwrapped blocks at 202-230. Behaviour holds under a wrapper; the claim does not. Class: evidence-overstatement.\n\n**F007 - The fold comment was left mid-sentence by the reflow** - `command-attach.ts:427` and `:435` - the branch produced a 57-character line and a 148-character line in the block that states the fold contract. Lines 432 and 436 predate the branch and are older debt. Class: documentation-readability.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n**WS-1 (P1, first): keep a later request a request.**\n1. Add the two F001 prompts and the two F002 prompts as failing-first rows.\n2. Move the `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` return below `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN`, or make the pronoun-request check win when both match.\n3. Bound `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` at `it` or a sentence boundary.\n4. Re-run `REQUEST6`, `CONTROL5` and the wrapper matrix; all must stay requests.\n\n**WS-2 (P2): close the reader-shape gaps.** Handle `](` before the fold, and read a post-name question clause or the pre-name decline vocabulary after the name.\n\n**WS-3 (P2): align the packet text.** Amend `spec.md:85`/`REQ-001` and `tasks.md:131`, or move the two rows into `PLAIN_ROWS`.\n\n**WS-4 (P2): re-wrap `command-attach.ts:421-436`.**\n\nP2 advisories are separate from WS-1 and do not gate the verdict on their own.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The document bullet must state the determiner condition, or the code must accept an article-less doc naming. Pick one; do not leave both readings live.\n- The tail-refusal rule needs a stated boundary: a refusal of `it` that ends the clause, versus a negation that qualifies it.\n- A link label and a doc path are two different things; the fold should not merge a label with a URL.\n- The checklist coverage claim should name the rows it covers, because a reader closes the packet on that sentence.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Failing-first rows for all four P1 prompts, then the three code edits in WS-1, WS-2.\n- A wrapper row for a linked label and a post-name question, so the two shapes stay pinned.\n- A spec/tasks text edit for F005 and F006, with the acceptance row quoting the determiner if the code keeps it.\n- Re-run the guards suite and the mention fixtures after the edits; `REQUEST6`, `CONTROL5` and `AC-001`'s five prompts are the regression floor.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | F005: `spec.md:85`/`REQ-001` vs `command-attach.ts:458`. All other scope bullets match (fold marks at 440-441, doc-path skip at 451, typed boundary at 208). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | F006: `tasks.md:131`. `AC-001` met on its five prompts and on `REQUEST6`/`CONTROL5`; `CHK-FIX-001` holds; `AC-005` is `Unmet` because this pass found P1s; `AC-004` is `Waived` by ADR-001 in the data area. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in the diff. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `plan.md:70` names the guards test and the matrix as verification; F001, F002 and F006 are outside it. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | The playbook row belongs to the data area. |\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: advisory-shortfall. The packet is Level 2 with `acceptance-criteria.md` present; AC-001 to AC-003 are Met, AC-004 is Waived (ADR-001), AC-005 is Unmet because this pass found two P1s. The signal is advisory and does not change the verdict.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- `AC-002`'s suite-wide claim (2381 passed) is unverified here: this lineage runs no suite and writes no test output.\n- The pre-existing comment orphan at `command-attach.ts:432` and the long line at 436 are older debt, outside this branch's diff.\n- The `data` area (intent phrases, the playbook prompt, ADR-001) is `data-13`'s; nothing here rules on it.\n- The open P2 of review passes ten to twelve and the `038-alignment-p1-remediation` list were not re-reported.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Swept directions: none.\n- Recovery: one stuck-recovery activation at iteration 6 (`stuckThresholdReached`), answered by a line-level security pass at iteration 7.\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- `searchCoverage`: no reducer-owned search-debt rows; `searchDebtCount` 0.\n- `candidateCoverage`: not applicable to this review (no required bug-class list on the lineage).\n- `searchLedger` rows were not produced: the lineage recorded classification and ruled-out rows in each delta instead.\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: bracketed-form occurrence loss, typed-boundary regression, pre-name decline regression, ReDoS, homoglyph bypass, fold DoS, reader mark-set divergence, stale citations, stale typed-reader comment.\n- `cleanSearchProof`: each ruled-out direction names the probe and its result in its iteration file (iterations 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7).\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- **Convergence summary**: iterations 1 to 7 recorded ratios 1.0, 0.14, 0.0, 0.07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0. Decisions: CONTINUE (1, 2, 3), CONTINUE (4), CONTINUE (5), STUCK_RECOVERY (6), CONTINUE (7). Terminal stop at iteration 8: `maxIterationsReached`, blocked by `dimensionCoverageGate`.\n- **Coverage summary**: correctness (iterations 1, 5, 8), traceability (2, 8), security (3, 7), maintainability (4, 6). All four dimensions covered; both scope files reviewed under every dimension.\n- **Graph**: a `SLICE` node for the mention area, `FILE` nodes for both scope files, per-dimension nodes, finding and evidence nodes, and `COVERS`/`IN_DIMENSION`/`IN_FILE`/`EVIDENCE_FOR`/`CONFIRMS` edges, persisted per iteration through `upsert.cjs` into the lineage's own graph directory.\n- **Ruled-out claims**: listed in section 9.\n- **Sources reviewed**: `command-attach.ts` (whole file plus four focused ranges), `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (whole file plus three ranges), `fusion.ts:1200-1216`, `review-brief-13.txt`, `review-scope-13.txt`, `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `command-offer-fit-gates.md`, and the old tree at `b8ebee37d75` for the comment comparison.\n- **State integrity**: 8 iteration rows across 7 runs; run 3 re-recorded with `findingsCount: 6` so its summary reads as the running total, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line rewritten to that record. Registry: 7 open, 0 resolved, all four dimensions covered.\n- **Write surface**: every artifact lives under `review/lineages/mention-13`. The only outside path with a fresh mtime is `review/observability-events.jsonl`, whose rows name `producer: fanout-run` and this lineage's label, so it is the parent runner's heartbeat.\n- **Continuity save**: not run. This lineage is forbidden from running `generate-context.js`, so continuity is left to the parent fan-out closeout.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - command mention pass thirteen (mention-13)\\n\\n- Session: `fanout-mention-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, generation 1, lineage `mention-13`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), mention area\\n- Scope files: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\\n- Diff reviewed: `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437`\\n- Iterations: 7 dispatched passes (8 iteration rows; run 3 was re-recorded), stop reason `maxIterationsReached`\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n**Overall verdict: FAIL.** The registry verdict is CONDITIONAL (0 P0, 2 P1, 5 P2), and the required coverage gate failed at the terminal stop (`traceability-incomplete`), which makes the session verdict FAIL under the review contract. No P0 was found; nothing here is an incident, and nothing here is a clean close either.\\n\\n`hasAdvisories: false` (the flag is only set on PASS).\\n\\nThe counts the verdict used: **P0 0, P1 2, P2 5**.\\n\\nWhat the two P1s say, in one line each:\\n\\n1. A command named as a document now reads as a mention even when the same prompt then asks to run it, so `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` loses the command the reader typed (F001).\\n2. A limiting negation after the name now reads as a refusal, so `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` loses the command too (F002).\\n\\nBoth sit in the request direction the packet names as a High risk (`spec.md:150`), and both were introduced by this branch's two new tail rules. The five P2s are two more reader-shape gaps, one spec text wider than the code, one checklist claim wider than the matrix, and one reflowed comment.\\n\\nWhy the coverage gate failed: the two core traceability protocols stay `partial` because F005 (the spec bullet) and F006 (the checklist claim) are packet-text defects that a read-only lineage cannot repair. The loop therefore ran to the 8-iteration cap instead of converging, and the gate that stops a run from closing over an overstated checklist did its job.\\n\\nSelf-check outcomes: both P1s carry typed claim-adjudication packets and were confirmed, not downgraded. No P0 candidate arose, so no Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass was owed. F007 was narrowed in iteration 6 after `git show b8ebee37d75` showed two of the four comment lines it first blamed predate the branch.\\n\\nOperator review focus, verbatim: `Review pass thirteen. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.`\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` **is required**: two active P1 findings plus a failing required gate.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": {\\n    \\\"P0\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P1\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"P2\\\": 5,\\n    \\\"ids\\\": [\\\"F001\\\", \\\"F002\\\", \\\"F003\\\", \\\"F004\\\", \\\"F005\\\", \\\"F006\\\", \\\"F007\\\"]\\n  },\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-1\\\",\\n      \\\"priority\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Keep a later request a request\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F001\\\", \\\"F002\\\"],\\n      \\\"surface\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-2\\\",\\n      \\\"priority\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Close the two reader-shape gaps\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F003\\\", \\\"F004\\\"],\\n      \\\"surface\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-3\\\",\\n      \\\"priority\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Align the packet text and checklist evidence with the code\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F005\\\", \\\"F006\\\"],\\n      \\\"surface\\\": \\\"040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md, 040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-4\\\",\\n      \\\"priority\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Re-wrap the fold comment\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F007\\\"],\\n      \\\"surface\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add the determiner condition to the document bullet in spec.md §3 and to REQ-001, or widen the code to accept an article-less doc naming.\\\",\\n    \\\"Restate CHK-FIX-002 so it names the leads the invariance matrix actually runs, or move the two new rows into PLAIN_ROWS.\\\",\\n    \\\"Record that a later request clause outranks a document naming, and that a qualified negation (`don't run it twice`) is a limit rather than a refusal.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add a failing-first test for `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` and for `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff`.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add a failing-first test for `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget`.\\\",\\n    \\\"Move the COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT return after the COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN check, or let the pronoun-request check win.\\\",\\n    \\\"Bound COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN to a clause that ends at `it` or continues with a sentence boundary.\\\",\\n    \\\"Drop the `](target)` pair (or treat `](` as a boundary) before the fold, so a markdown link label keeps its own occurrence.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add the two new rows to PLAIN_ROWS, or narrow the CHK-FIX-002 sentence to the leads the matrix runs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Re-wrap comment lines 421-436 to the block width.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"logic-ordering\\\", \\\"logic-overreach\\\", \\\"normalization-edge\\\", \\\"vocabulary-asymmetry\\\", \\\"spec-drift\\\", \\\"evidence-overstatement\\\", \\\"documentation-readability\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### P1 - Required\\n\\n**F001 - A document naming returns a mention before a later request clause is read**\\n- Dimension: correctness. File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:458`.\\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` returns `true` before the `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` check at line 460. The contract at lines 403-407 says a use-verb clause with `it` turns an earlier naming into a request.\\n- Impact: `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` yields `typedCommandForTop(...) === undefined`; `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff` yields `attachCommand(...) === undefined` even though `thorough` matches `DEPTH_REQUEST`.\\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: logic-ordering.\\n- Scope proof: exported guards and consumer run on both prompts; both classify as mentions, and the unchanged pronoun regex matches the tail `command file, then run it`, so the earlier read was a request.\\n- Affected surface hints: `command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\\n- Fix: move the document return after the pronoun-request check, or let a use-verb clause win.\\n\\n**F002 - A limiting negation after the name reads as a refusal**\\n- Dimension: correctness. File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413`.\\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` ends at `it\\\\b`, so any qualifier after `it` still refuses.\\n- Impact: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` lose the typed command.\\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: logic-overreach.\\n- Scope proof: both prompts classify as mentions; the unchanged lead tests cannot produce that reading, so `b8ebee37d75` returned a request.\\n- Affected surface hints: `command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\\n- Fix: bound the tail refusal at `it` or a sentence boundary.\\n\\n### P2 - Advisories\\n\\n**F003 - A markdown link label abuts its target and the naming stops being an occurrence** - `command-attach.ts:441` - the fold drops brackets and parentheses, so `[/create:readme](https://example.com/docs)` merges into `/create:readmehttps://...`, the lookahead at 451 rejects it and `occurrences.length === 0` returns `false`. `do not run [/create:readme](https://example.com/docs) yet` therefore offers `/create:readme`. Class: normalization-edge.\\n\\n**F004 - The post-name reader covers one clause shape** - `command-attach.ts:459` - a question (`/create:readme, what does it do?`) and a sibling refusal (`/create:readme is wrong, skip it`) still read as requests and offer the command. Class: vocabulary-asymmetry.\\n\\n**F005 - The spec's document bullet is wider than the code's determiner rule** - `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:85` - the bullet and `REQ-001` (`spec.md:119`) state the document shape without a determiner; the code requires `the|this|that` at `command-attach.ts:458`. `read /create:readme documentation and tell me what it does` still offers the command. `tasks.md:46` records the narrowing as deliberate, so the packet text is the stale part. Class: spec-drift.\\n\\n**F006 - CHK-FIX-002 claims matrix coverage for leads the matrix never wraps** - `040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:131` - `PLAIN_ROWS` (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:179-182`) holds only the older fixtures, while `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` and `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` appear only in the unwrapped blocks at 202-230. Behaviour holds under a wrapper; the claim does not. Class: evidence-overstatement.\\n\\n**F007 - The fold comment was left mid-sentence by the reflow** - `command-attach.ts:427` and `:435` - the branch produced a 57-character line and a 148-character line in the block that states the fold contract. Lines 432 and 436 predate the branch and are older debt. Class: documentation-readability.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n**WS-1 (P1, first): keep a later request a request.**\\n1. Add the two F001 prompts and the two F002 prompts as failing-first rows.\\n2. Move the `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` return below `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN`, or make the pronoun-request check win when both match.\\n3. Bound `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` at `it` or a sentence boundary.\\n4. Re-run `REQUEST6`, `CONTROL5` and the wrapper matrix; all must stay requests.\\n\\n**WS-2 (P2): close the reader-shape gaps.** Handle `](` before the fold, and read a post-name question clause or the pre-name decline vocabulary after the name.\\n\\n**WS-3 (P2): align the packet text.** Amend `spec.md:85`/`REQ-001` and `tasks.md:131`, or move the two rows into `PLAIN_ROWS`.\\n\\n**WS-4 (P2): re-wrap `command-attach.ts:421-436`.**\\n\\nP2 advisories are separate from WS-1 and do not gate the verdict on their own.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The document bullet must state the determiner condition, or the code must accept an article-less doc naming. Pick one; do not leave both readings live.\\n- The tail-refusal rule needs a stated boundary: a refusal of `it` that ends the clause, versus a negation that qualifies it.\\n- A link label and a doc path are two different things; the fold should not merge a label with a URL.\\n- The checklist coverage claim should name the rows it covers, because a reader closes the packet on that sentence.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Failing-first rows for all four P1 prompts, then the three code edits in WS-1, WS-2.\\n- A wrapper row for a linked label and a post-name question, so the two shapes stay pinned.\\n- A spec/tasks text edit for F005 and F006, with the acceptance row quoting the determiner if the code keeps it.\\n- Re-run the guards suite and the mention fixtures after the edits; `REQUEST6`, `CONTROL5` and `AC-001`'s five prompts are the regression floor.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | F005: `spec.md:85`/`REQ-001` vs `command-attach.ts:458`. All other scope bullets match (fold marks at 440-441, doc-path skip at 451, typed boundary at 208). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | F006: `tasks.md:131`. `AC-001` met on its five prompts and on `REQUEST6`/`CONTROL5`; `CHK-FIX-001` holds; `AC-005` is `Unmet` because this pass found P1s; `AC-004` is `Waived` by ADR-001 in the data area. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in the diff. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No runtime mirror is touched. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `plan.md:70` names the guards test and the matrix as verification; F001, F002 and F006 are outside it. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | The playbook row belongs to the data area. |\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: advisory-shortfall. The packet is Level 2 with `acceptance-criteria.md` present; AC-001 to AC-003 are Met, AC-004 is Waived (ADR-001), AC-005 is Unmet because this pass found two P1s. The signal is advisory and does not change the verdict.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- `AC-002`'s suite-wide claim (2381 passed) is unverified here: this lineage runs no suite and writes no test output.\\n- The pre-existing comment orphan at `command-attach.ts:432` and the long line at 436 are older debt, outside this branch's diff.\\n- The `data` area (intent phrases, the playbook prompt, ADR-001) is `data-13`'s; nothing here rules on it.\\n- The open P2 of review passes ten to twelve and the `038-alignment-p1-remediation` list were not re-reported.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Swept directions: none.\\n- Recovery: one stuck-recovery activation at iteration 6 (`stuckThresholdReached`), answered by a line-level security pass at iteration 7.\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- `searchCoverage`: no reducer-owned search-debt rows; `searchDebtCount` 0.\\n- `candidateCoverage`: not applicable to this review (no required bug-class list on the lineage).\\n- `searchLedger` rows were not produced: the lineage recorded classification and ruled-out rows in each delta instead.\\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: bracketed-form occurrence loss, typed-boundary regression, pre-name decline regression, ReDoS, homoglyph bypass, fold DoS, reader mark-set divergence, stale citations, stale typed-reader comment.\\n- `cleanSearchProof`: each ruled-out direction names the probe and its result in its iteration file (iterations 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7).\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- **Convergence summary**: iterations 1 to 7 recorded ratios 1.0, 0.14, 0.0, 0.07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0. Decisions: CONTINUE (1, 2, 3), CONTINUE (4), CONTINUE (5), STUCK_RECOVERY (6), CONTINUE (7). Terminal stop at iteration 8: `maxIterationsReached`, blocked by `dimensionCoverageGate`.\\n- **Coverage summary**: correctness (iterations 1, 5, 8), traceability (2, 8), security (3, 7), maintainability (4, 6). All four dimensions covered; both scope files reviewed under every dimension.\\n- **Graph**: a `SLICE` node for the mention area, `FILE` nodes for both scope files, per-dimension nodes, finding and evidence nodes, and `COVERS`/`IN_DIMENSION`/`IN_FILE`/`EVIDENCE_FOR`/`CONFIRMS` edges, persisted per iteration through `upsert.cjs` into the lineage's own graph directory.\\n- **Ruled-out claims**: listed in section 9.\\n- **Sources reviewed**: `command-attach.ts` (whole file plus four focused ranges), `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (whole file plus three ranges), `fusion.ts:1200-1216`, `review-brief-13.txt`, `review-scope-13.txt`, `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `command-offer-fit-gates.md`, and the old tree at `b8ebee37d75` for the comment comparison.\\n- **State integrity**: 8 iteration rows across 7 runs; run 3 re-recorded with `findingsCount: 6` so its summary reads as the running total, and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line rewritten to that record. Registry: 7 open, 0 resolved, all four dimensions covered.\\n- **Write surface**: every artifact lives under `review/lineages/mention-13`. The only outside path with a fresh mtime is `review/observability-events.jsonl`, whose rows name `producer: fanout-run` and this lineage's label, so it is the parent runner's heartbeat.\\n- **Continuity save**: not run. This lineage is forbidden from running `generate-context.js`, so continuity is left to the parent fan-out closeout.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794867265934,"end":1794867305315}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794867306534,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"id":"prt_1e66da026001J7Cdt9YmcZ32Wf","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e66cd9da001kfbGk974AssBZR","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"99d5334b581ed8d856f5483c58fbddd1f5f9cfb3","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":652,"output":4577,"reasoning":280,"cache":{"read":319744,"write":0}}}}
