{"type":"text","timestamp":1794867409936,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","part":{"id":"prt_1e66f1c6a001Ej0BNAn21SOgb6","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffeS7sVTvhEMa7jvO","messageID":"msg_1e66f1247001bhTzFoxs3WDuII","type":"text","text":"**Verdict: FAIL.** No P0; two P1 findings and five P2, plus a required gate failing at the stop, so the session verdict is FAIL while the registry verdict is CONDITIONAL.\n\n**What the review found**\n\n1. **F001 (P1)** `command-attach.ts:458`: the new document rule returns \"mention\" before the existing later-request rule runs. `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` loses the command the reader typed; so does a \"read the docs, then do a thorough review\" prompt, even though `thorough` matches the depth gate.\n2. **F002 (P1)** `command-attach.ts:413`: the new tail refusal ends at `it`, so a limiting negation reads as a refusal. `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` lose their commands. This is the exact High risk the packet records at `spec.md:150`.\n3. **P2s**: a markdown link label merges with its URL and the naming stops being an occurrence (F003); the post-name reader covers one clause shape, so a question or `skip it` still reads as a request (F004); the spec's document bullet is wider than the code's determiner rule (F005); `CHK-FIX-002` claims matrix coverage the matrix never runs (F006); the fold comment's reflowed lines (F007).\n\n**Why it stopped at the cap, not convergence**: `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence` stay partial because F005 and F006 are packet-text defects a read-only lineage cannot fix, so the coverage gate vetoed STOP and the loop used all 8 iterations. One stuck-recovery activation at iteration 6 was answered by a line-level security pass at iteration 7.\n\n**Artifacts** (all under `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13`): 8 iteration files and deltas, a 21-row ledger with per-iteration graph and stop events, the reducer's registry and dashboard, `review-report.md` with all nine sections plus the Planning Packet, and config marked complete. All 8 iterations pass `verify-iteration.cjs`. No file outside the lineage was written by this process; the one outside path with a fresh mtime is the parent runner's own heartbeat log.\n\nOne disclosed repair: run 3's record was re-issued with `findingsCount: 6` and `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`'s first line rewritten, because the first version's zero count plus a running summary made the reducer pad six phantom findings.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:mention-13","time":{"start":1794867403882,"end":1794867409936}}}
